.TH NUCLEUSFLOW 1 "October 2026" "NucleusFlow 0.0.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nucleusflow \- A modern, memory-safe static site generator written in Rust
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nucleusflow
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI<COMMAND>\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
NucleusFlow is a high-performance, memory-safe static site generator and content
processing pipeline written in Rust. It prioritises security with strict input
sanitisation, path traversal rejection, and deterministic content generation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose logging (\-v, \-vv, \-vvv).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help information.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBnew\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI<NAME>\fR
Create a new static site project.
.RS
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Name of the new project directory.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
Starter template to use (\fIblog\fR, \fIdocs\fR, \fIportfolio\fR). Default is \fIblog\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fBbuild\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Build the static site from markdown content and Handlebars templates.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-content-dir\fR \fI<CONTENT_DIR>\fR
Path to content directory. Default is \fIcontent\fR.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output-dir\fR \fI<OUTPUT_DIR>\fR
Path to output directory. Default is \fIpublic\fR.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-template-dir\fR \fI<TEMPLATE_DIR>\fR
Path to template directory. Default is \fItemplates\fR.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-minify\fR
Enable HTML minification of output files.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Build configuration file. Default is \fInucleusflow.toml\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fBserve\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Start the embedded development preview server.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
Port to serve on. Default is \fI3000\fR.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-watch\fR
Enable file watching and live reloading.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Base directory to serve files from. Default is \fIpublic\fR.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create a new blog project:
.B nucleusflow new mysite --template blog
.TP
Build static output with minification:
.B nucleusflow build --minify
.TP
Preview the built site on port 8080:
.B nucleusflow serve --port 8080 --dir public
